<title>SINGAPORE: Vikay first half net profit falls 93 pct.</title>
<headline>Vikay first half net profit falls 93 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of S$ unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		     0.08	vs    1.08</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)	 0.10	vs    0.90</p>
<p>    Turnover			47.69	vs   48.80</p>
<p>    Interest income		0.01	vs    0.04</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		 0.84	vs    1.15</p>
<p>    Interest on borrowings     2.33	vs    1.38</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation  2.07	vs    1.58</p>
<p>    Tax				nil	 vs    0.05</p>
<p>Note - Electronics-based Vikay Industrial Ltd said the drop in profits was due to higher interest costs on increased bank borrowings and higher operating costs. It expects additional products launched in the second half will improve results.</p>
<p>-- Singapore 65-8703080</p>
</text>
